      <section id="problem" class="alt">
        <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
          <p class="kicker">The problem</p>
          <h2>Usage limits stop the work, often hours before you're back.</h2>
          <div class="night">
            <p>It's 11 PM and your agent is halfway through a refactor. It stops: the usage limit resets at 3 AM. Nobody is there to type "continue", so the work waits.</p>
            <p>At 8 AM you open the laptop and find it exactly where it stopped, with the limit long since reset. With Rewake, the same session picks the work back up at 3:01 AM, and in the morning you find it further along. (For that, the computer has to be on and awake: <a href="#when">when it sends</a>.)</p>
          </div>
          <p class="sub">
            Coding agents run on plans with rolling limits. When one is reached mid-task, the agent stops, in an editor or in a terminal, and usually nothing picks the work back up: you have to come back after the reset and type something.
          </p>
          <div class="facts-row">
            <div class="fact">
              <q>You've hit your session limit · resets 3:45pm</q>
