          <h2>Where the other ways stop.</h2>
          <p class="sub">Rewake keeps one session going, across every agent you use, from one place. The ways people try instead each cover a corner of that. Checked {updated}.</p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">What it covers</th><th scope="col">Where it stops</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><b>Agent Rewake</b></td><td>Every external agent in Zed's Agent Panel, and the same session of Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot CLI, Gemini CLI, Grok Build, Qwen Code, OpenCode or Antigravity CLI (previews). One command, <code>/rewake</code>, and one page for every thread</td><td>The previews are early, and a closed session needs the computer on and awake. Rewake never approves a permission prompt for you</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Claude Code's own continue</td><td>Claude, in Claude Code's own terminal sessions</td><td>That one agent only, and nothing is scheduled: no message later, no repeat, no queue. It waits inside the session, so the terminal has to stay open; after the computer sleeps for more than half an hour it asks you to press Enter, and it re-arms at most twice in a row. Rewake steps aside when it handles a limit, and covers the agents and the cases it doesn't</td></tr>
